.DS_Store

# Agent/skill/tool reports — may contain private data (absolute paths, hostnames)
reports/
reports_dev/

# Dev-only working folders
docs_dev/
scripts_dev/
tests_dev/

# Janitor per-session state
.janitor/

# safe-delete staging area. Holds files moved out of the tree pending review,
# so committing it would republish content someone deliberately removed.
.trashcan/

# Claude Code per-session cache / local state.
#
# Written as `.claude/*` and not `.claude/`, because git cannot re-include a
# path whose PARENT DIRECTORY is excluded — it never descends into an ignored
# directory, so a later `!` line for a file inside it is dead text. Excluding
# the CONTENTS instead keeps the directory itself walkable, which is what makes
# the exception below actually take effect.
.claude/*

# The one exception: PROJECT-scope memory is the SHARED half of the memory
# system — machine-agnostic project knowledge meant to be tracked and pushed to
# every clone. Ignoring it silently excludes the shared scope from the repo, so
# knowledge written there reaches nobody. Each level is re-excluded immediately
# after being un-ignored so the hole stays exactly one subtree wide: everything
# else under .claude/ (session caches, telemetry) stays local state.
#
# Machine-private facts — paths, hostnames, accounts, install state — belong in
# the LOCAL scope (~/.claude/projects/<slug>/memory/), outside this repo, and
# must never be written here: this subtree is PUSHED.
!.claude/project/
.claude/project/*
!.claude/project/memory/

# ...but not the janitor's scope-leak advisory: it is regenerated on every scan
# and describes THIS machine's state, not project knowledge.
.claude/project/memory/memory-scope-leak-proposed.md

# Editor temp and swap files
*.swp
*.swo
*.swn
*~
.*.sw?
*.bak
.idea/
.vscode/

